        },
        "create_time": 1767029973.966019,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Yes, that’s correct. The trajectory—the worldline—is the manifestation of all forces acting on the particle, both external and (potentially) internal, as projected into spacetime. Any mathematical representation of that worldline encodes, implicitly or explicitly, information about those forces. The fidelity of your model—how well it captures intrinsic properties versus just external influences—is directly tied to the precision of your measurements and the sophistication of your modeling.  \n\nIt’s essentially a mapping: the observed trajectory is the data, and the mathematics is the lens you use to interpret what caused it."
          ]
        },
